abstract: >-
  Zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 six-kernel formalization (28 headline theorems T1a-T6c,
  29 Palomar Comparator targets, 45 axiom-audited declarations strictly within
  propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound) and tri-language Rust/ISO C11/Python
  differential verifiers covering six algebraic pillars across generalized
  Cayley-Dickson algebras CD_n(gamma): (1) universal all-n, all-signature Nilpotent
  Mirror Conservation, full bilinear 2-blade nilpotency, and the exact 2x2 block
  linear-algebra Z-basis isomorphism for ker L_{e_i + e_j} (T1a-T1f); (2) the
  Euclidean Dyadic-Palindromic Terrace Law, Moreno's 2-blade divisibility 4 | nu,
  attained ceiling 2^{n-1}-4 with BDI equality iff n=4 among n>=4, and the
  all-signature midpoint law H_n^gamma(2^{n-2}) = 42 * 2^{n-4} (T2a-T2f);
  (3) Euclidean coordinate right-multiplier clique number omega(G_n^comp) = n+5,
  breakaway below rho(2^n) at dimension 64 (11 < 12), and [2^{n-1}, 2(n+4), 2^n]
  doubling tower (T3a-T3d); (4) Sedenion Triple-42 duality (42 bad 2+2 planes,
  pure-product re-verification of de Marrais's 7xK_{2,2,2} box-kites, 42 maximal
  10D subspaces with Fano split 7+28+7), pure-kernel Pathion ceiling r_max(CD_5)=14
  with strict 7+7 half-balance rigidity across all 2^32 subsets retiring MILP from
  the proof trust base (T4e), and pure-kernel certification of CD_6(56) (T4f);
  (5) universal all-n Binary Reflected Gray-Code bit-locking of i xor j by nu/4 (T5a),
  exponentially wide continuous spectral band gaps of width 2^{n-3}-1 at flip = 2^n-8
  for every n >= 6 (T5b), and the exact all-n all-signature iff spectral-gap dichotomy
  counting 2^{n-3}-4 gapped signatures (T5c); and (6) universal all-n all-signature
  mod-2 twisted-group-algebra Frobenius involution (T6a), fraction-free odd-pivot
  integral matrix inversion excluding all odd-coordinate-sum integer zero divisors
  across every dimension and signature (T6b), and non-singularity of every signed
  odd-support unit k-blade (3-, 5-, 7-blades, ...) with zero-divisor parity
  conservation (T6c).
